89}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>(In trillions of dollars)</th><th>Social Security<sup>1</sup></th><th>Medicare HI<sup>1</sup></th><th>Medicare SMI<sup>1</sup></th><th>Other<sup>2</sup></th><th>Total</th></tr><tr><td>Net present value (NPV) of future revenue less future expenditures for current and future participants (the \\\"open group\\\") over the next 75 years, beginning of the year</td><td>(15.4)</td><td>(3.5)</td><td>(30.0)</td><td>(0.1)</td><td>(49.0)</td></tr><tr><td>Reasons for changes in the NPV during the year:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Changes in valuation period</td><td>(0.6)</td><td>(0.2)</td><td>(1.2)</td><td>-</td><td>(2.0)</td></tr><tr><td>Changes in demographic data, assumptions, and methods</td><td>0.1</td><td>0.4</td><td>0.2</td><td>-</td><td>0.7</td></tr><tr><td>Changes in economic data, assumptions, and methods</td><td>(0.5)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>(0.5)</td></tr><tr><td>Changes in law or policy</td><td>-</td><td>(0.5)</td><td>(0.5)</td><td>-</td><td>(1.0)</td></tr><tr><td>Changes in methodology and programmatic data</td><td>0.2</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>0.2</td></tr><tr><td>Changes in economic and other health care assumptions</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>(1.5)</td><td>-</td><td>(1.5)</td></tr><tr><td>Change in projection base</td><td>-</td><td>(0.9)</td><td>-</td><td>-</td><td>(0.9)</td></tr><tr><td>Net change in open group measure</td><td>(0.8)</td><td>(1.2)</td><td>(3.0)</td><td>-</td><td>(5.0)</td></tr><tr><td>Open group measure, end of year</td><td>(16.2)</td><td>(4.7)</td><td>(33.0)</td><td>(0.1)</td><td>(54.0)</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 1091, 889, 1117], \"page_id\": 89}], \"content\": \"Amounts represent changes between valuation dates 1/1/2017 and 1/1/2018.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [149, 1127, 1472, 1188], \"page_id\": 89}], \"content\": \"Includes Railroad Retirement changes between valuation dates 10/1/2016 and 10/1/2017 and Black Lung changes between 9/30/2017 and 9/30/2018.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1233, 854, 1256], \"page_id\": 89}], \"content\": \"The accompanying notes are an integral part of these financial statements.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 1273, 849, 1299], \"page_id\": 89}], \"content\": \"Previously reported amounts have been adjusted for rounding differences.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1379, 1994, 1490, 2018], \"page_id\": 89}], \"content\": \"March 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 94, 178, 130], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"84\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [714, 127, 916, 156], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [388, 205, 1246, 255], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Airport and Airway Trust Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 269, 789, 516], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"The Airport and Airway Trust Fund was established on the books of the Department of Treasury in fiscal year 1971, according to provisions of the Airport and Airway Revenue Act of 1970 [49 United States Code 1742(a), repealed]. The Tax Equity and Fiscal Responsibility Act of 1982 (Public Law 97-248, dated September 3, 1982) reestablished the trust fund in the Internal Revenue Code (26 United States Code 9502) effective September 1, 1982.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 519, 790, 759], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Treasury transfers from the general fund to the trust fund amounts equivalent to the taxes received from transportation of persons and property by air, gasoline and jet fuel used in commercial and noncommercial aircraft, and an international arrival and departure tax. The Omnibus Budget Reconciliation Act of 1990 (Public Law 101-508, dated November 5, 1990) increased rates for the excise taxes transferred to the fund.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 764, 789, 976], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Treasury bases these transfers on estimates made by the Secretary of the Treasury. These are subject to adjustments in later transfers in the amount of actual tax receipts. The FAA Reauthorization Act of 2018 (Public Law 115-254), effective October 5, 2018, extended the aviation excise taxes until October 1, 2023. The Act included provisions that:\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 978, 790, 1226], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing passenger ticket, flight segment, and freight waybill taxes. The domestic flight segment tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2019, the tax is $4.30. It also retained a special rule applied to flights between the continental United States and Alaska or Hawaii. This departure tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2019, the tax is $9.50.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1235, 790, 1358], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing tax per person for international flights that begin or end in the United States. The tax is indexed to the Consumer Price Index; effective calendar year 2019, the tax is $18.90.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 276, 1490, 464], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Retained the existing tax on payments to airlines for frequent flyer and similar awards by banks and credit card companies, merchants and frequent flyer program partners, such as other airlines, hotels and rental car companies, and other businesses. The tax on mileage awards is 7.5% of the value of the miles.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 469, 1494, 622], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Retained the commercial aviation fuel tax and the general aviation jet fuel/gas taxes. The current tax rate for commercial aviation fuel is 4.3 cents per gallon and 19.3 cents per gallon for general aviation gas. General aviation jet fuel is 21.8 cents per gallon.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 622, 1494, 865], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"The FAA Modernization and Reform Act 2012 imposed a new surtax on fuel used in aircraft that is part of a fractional ownership program; the surtax applies to fuel used after March 31, 2012. Currently this is a 14.1 cents per gallon surcharge of fuel used in fractional ownership flights. It also changed the classification of transportation as part of a fractional ownership program from commercial aviation to noncommercial aviation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 867, 1492, 1054], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"The FAA Modernization and Reform Act 2012 also repealed the excise tax exemption for transportation by small jet aircraft operating on non-established lines. (IRS defines the term \\\"operated on an established line\\\" to mean operated with some degree of regularity between definite points).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 1054, 1494, 1143], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"More recently, however, P.L. 115-97 exempts certain payments related to the management of private aircraft from the excise taxes imposed on taxable transportation by air.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 1143, 1494, 1362], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"Treasury makes available to the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), Department of Transportation (DOT), amounts required for outlays to carry out the Airport and Airway program. The Secretary of the Treasury makes other charges to the trust fund to transfer certain refunds of taxes and certain outfits, under section 34 of the Internal Revenue Code (IRC).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1994, 259, 2020], \"page_id\": 90}], \"content\": \"March 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [710, 90, 918, 132], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1441, 85, 1497, 130], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"85\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [475, 179, 1158, 271], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-1.\\u2014Airport and Airway Trust Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2019\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [747, 280, 883, 309], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"(Source: DOT)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 311, 1488, 1289], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Description</th><th>IRC section (26 United States Code)</th><th>Amount</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2018</td><td></td><td>$16,982,000,000</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Receipts:</td></tr><tr><td>Grants-in-aid for Airports funding from General Fund</td><td></td><td>1,000,000,000</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Excise taxes (transferred from general fund):</td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel in a fractional ownership flight</td><td>4043</td><td>17,744,374</td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel other than gasoline</td><td>4041</td><td>649,328,558</td></tr><tr><td>Gasoline</td><td>4081</td><td>27,966,107</td></tr><tr><td>Transportation by airseats, berths, etc.</td><td>4261 (a) (b)</td><td>10,365,106,438</td></tr><tr><td>Use of international travel facilities</td><td>4261 (c)</td><td>4,281,268,137</td></tr><tr><td>Transportation of property, cargo</td><td>4271</td><td>650,373,607</td></tr><tr><td>Gross excise taxes</td><td></td><td>15,991,787,222</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Less refunds of taxes (reimbursed to general fund):</td></tr><tr><td>Liquid fuel other than gasoline</td><td>4041</td><td>11,007,466</td></tr><tr><td>Gasoline</td><td></td><td>4,792,575</td></tr><tr><td>Total refunds of taxes</td><td></td><td>15,800,041</td></tr><tr><td>Net taxes</td><td></td><td>15,975,987,180</td></tr><tr><td>General Fund Payments</td><td></td><td>500,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Refunds on Federal Payments (DOT)</td><td></td><td>24,849,772</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td></td><td>343,001,731</td></tr><tr><td>CMIA interest income</td><td></td><td>11,491</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td></td><td>16,843,850,176</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"3\\\">Expenses:</td></tr><tr><td>Operations</td><td></td><td>9,250,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>Grants in aid for Airports</td><td></td><td>3,466,815,069</td></tr><tr><td>Facilities and equipment</td><td></td><td>2,924,126,296</td></tr><tr><td>Research, engineering, and development</td><td></td><td>161,557,944</td></tr><tr><td>Air carriers</td><td></td><td>196,974,136</td></tr><tr><td>CMIA Interest Expense</td><td></td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Total expenses</td><td></td><td>15,999,473,446</td></tr><tr><td>Offsetting collections</td><td></td><td>89,320,307</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30, 2019</td><td></td><td>$17,915,697,036</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [133, 1325, 521, 1355], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Detail may not add to totals due to rounding.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [322, 1412, 1308, 1490], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"Airport and Airway Trust Fund\\nExpected Condition and Results of Operations, Fiscal Years 2020-2024\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [676, 1494, 945, 1530], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars. Source: DOT)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 1527, 1490, 1893], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th></th><th>2020</th><th>2021</th><th>2022</th><th>2023</th><th>2024</th></tr><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1</td><td>17,916</td><td>17,668</td><td>17,813</td><td>18,957</td><td>21,066</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Excise taxes, net of refunds</td><td>17,440</td><td>17,987</td><td>18,933</td><td>19,940</td><td>21,123</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>426</td><td>375</td><td>507</td><td>562</td><td>653</td></tr><tr><td>Offsetting collections</td><td>100</td><td>100</td><td>140</td><td>143</td><td>153</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>17,966</td><td>18,462</td><td>19,580</td><td>20,645</td><td>21,929</td></tr><tr><td>Expenses:</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Gross Outlays</td><td>18,214</td><td>18,317</td><td>18,436</td><td>18,536</td><td>18,779</td></tr><tr><td>Balance Sept. 30</td><td>17,668</td><td>17,813</td><td>18,957</td><td>21,066</td><td>24,216</td></tr></table>\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"table\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1362, 1982, 1506, 2025], \"page_id\": 91}], \"content\": \"March 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 97, 182, 127], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"86\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [719, 94, 918, 130], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [337, 189, 1286, 283], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning (D&D) Fund\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 297, 803, 603], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"The Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund was established on the books of the Treasury in fiscal year (FY) 1993, in accordance with provisions of the Energy Policy Act of 1992 (42 United States Code 2297g). Receipts represent (1) fees collected from domestic public utilities based on their pro rata share of purchases of separative work units from the Department of Energy (DOE) and (2) appropriations toward the Government contribution based on the balance of separative work unit purchases.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 610, 805, 896], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Expenditures from the fund include (1) decontaminating and decommissioning three gaseous diffusion plants (Oak Ridge, Tennessee; Paducah, Kentucky; and Portsmouth, Ohio), (2) remedial actions and related environmental restoration cost at the gaseous diffusion plants, and (3) reimbursement to uranium/thorium producers for the cost of decontamination, decommissioning, reclamation, and remedial action of uranium/thorium sites that are incident to sales to the U. S. Government.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 910, 803, 1160], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Amounts available in the fund exceeding current needs may be invested by the Secretary of the Treasury in obligations of the United States (1) having maturities consistent with the needs of the fund and (2) bearing interest at rates determined appropriate, taking into consideration the current average market yield on outstanding marketable obligations of the United States with remaining periods to maturity comparable to these investments.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1174, 809, 1365], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"Annually, the Secretary of the Treasury, after consultation with the Secretary of Energy, is required to provide a report to Congress (see 42 USC 2297g(b)(1)). This report must present the financial condition and the results of operations of the fund during the preceding fiscal year.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 292, 1497, 603], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"The Energy Policy Act of 1992 (42 USC 2297g-1, as amended) authorized annual deposits to the fund of $518.2 million (before adjustments for inflation) over a 15-year period. Funding was provided by fees assessed on domestic public utilities that purchased enriched uranium and Government contributions. As specified in the Act, annual assessments from domestic public utilities (before adjustment for inflation) were not to exceed $150 million. The Government was responsible for the remainder ($369.6 million), adjusted for inflation.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [834, 620, 1501, 1174], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"While the final utility assessments occurred in (FY) 2007, during the same period (i.e., between FYs 1993 and 2007), the Government contributed only $5,362.4 million of the $6,281.0 million specified in the Act. This resulted in a $918.6 million shortfall of the authorized Government contributions. The Government continued to make annual contributions to eliminate this shortfall. Through the FY 2009 contribution, the overall shortfall (after adjusting for inflation) was $40.6 million. Also, during FY 2009, the Government designated $390 million of American Recovery and Reinvestment Act (ARRA) funding for the Fund's mission. While ARRA funding was not an actual deposit into the fund's invested balances, it provided a dollar-for-dollar reduction in the required outlays from the invested balances. The Department of Energy recognized the ARRA funding as an offset to the Government's contribution shortfall, thereby, satisfying the Government's contribution responsibility.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 1183, 1490, 1315], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"The last appropriation was made in FY 2017 when Congress appropriated $563 Million. In FY 2018, Congress authorized the transfer of about $860.6 million in balances from a related account.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 1992, 266, 2020], \"page_id\": 92}], \"content\": \"March 2020\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"page_footer\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [723, 101, 914, 125], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"TRUST FUNDS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1457, 101, 1488, 125], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"87\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [240, 200, 1397, 269], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"TABLE TF-2.\\u2014Uranium Enrichment Decontamination and Decommissioning Fund Results of Operations, Fiscal Year 2019\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [765, 285, 867, 302], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"(Source: DOE)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 321, 1490, 1009], \"page_id\": 93}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><td>Balance Oct. 1, 2018</td><td>$9,705,973.86</td></tr><tr><td>Receipts:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Fees collected</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Penalties collected</td><td>-</td></tr><tr><td>Interest on investments</td><td>60,951,899.05</td></tr><tr><td>Total receipts</td><td>60,951,899.05</td></tr><tr><td>Nonexpenditure transfers:</td><td></td></tr><tr><td