{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346210-g63IUcCSQY06bYjznDZe","role":"assistant","created":1775346220,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's no table with explicit quarter data in the JSON. Let me think about this differently. The text mentions \"quarterly percent change at annual rate\" which is the standard way the Bureau of Economic Analysis reports quarterly GDP growth. This is the data I need.\n\nThe question is asking for:\n- \"U.S. quarterly growth rates of the real GDP at 'unannualized' values that are actually reported as annual rate values rounded to the nearest tenths place from CY 2013-2019\"\n\nThis seems like a contradiction or tricky wording. Let me parse it:\n- \"unannualized values\" - this would be the quarter-over-quarter growth rate expressed as a percent\n- \"that are actually reported as annual rate values\" - but the data is reported as annual rates (seasonally adjusted annualized rates - SAAR)\n\nSo I think what they're asking for is: the quarterly GDP growth rates as they are typically reported (as annualized percentages), but we need to find the \"unannualized\" versions (the actual quarterly growth rates). \n\nActually wait, let me re-read: \"at 'unannualized' values that are actually reported as annual rate values\"\n\nHmm, this could mean the values are reported as annual rates but should be considered \"unannualized\" for the purpose of this calculation. Or it could mean the reverse.\n\nActually, I think the simplest interpretation is:\n- We use the quarterly growth rates that ARE reported (as annual rates)\n- These are \"unannualized\" in the sense that they're the quarterly rates (not annual)\n- They are rounded to the nearest tenth\n\nThe typical data is:\n- Q1 2013: 2.9% (annual rate)\n- Q2 2013: 1.8%\n- etc.\n\nLet me look for more complete data. The Treasury Bulletin might have more data. Let me also check the 2016 bulletin for more historical data.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_733f6eb8a8c342dca46b181c","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me check for BEA or GDP data in the text\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2020_03.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Find all GDP percentage mentions with quarter info\n# Look for patterns like \"X.X percent at an annual rate\" with quarter info\npattern = r'(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*(?:percent|%) at an annual rate'\nmatches = re.findall(pattern, content)\nprint(\"Annual rate percentages found:\", matches[:20])\n\n# Look for quarter references near GDP\npattern2 = r'(Q[1-4]|first quarter|second quarter|third quarter|fourth quarter).*?(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*(?:percent|%).*?annual rate'\nmatches2 = re.findall(pattern2, content, re.IGNORECASE)\nprint(\"\\nQuarterly GDP growth (annual rate):\")\nfor m in matches2[:20]:\n    print(f\"  {m[0]}: {m[1]}%\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
