{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346234-MALrTw69qZUjuLLc3uu2","role":"assistant","created":1775346245,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on my extensive analysis of the treasury bulletin documents, I've found that they contain narrative text about GDP growth but not the specific quarterly GDP data tables needed to answer the question.\n\nLet me reconsider the question. It asks for:\n- \"U.S. quarterly growth rates of the real GDP at 'unannualized' values that are actually reported as annual rate values rounded to the nearest tenths place\"\n- From CY 2013-2019 inclusive\n\nThe phrase \"unannualized values that are actually reported as annual rate values\" is a bit confusing, but it seems to refer to quarterly GDP growth rates that are reported at annualized rates (like \"2.1 percent at an annual rate\").\n\nThe documents provide narrative descriptions of GDP growth for some quarters, but I don't see complete quarterly data for all of 2013-2019. \n\nLet me check if there's another source - perhaps I should look more carefully at the treasury bulletins to see if there are any GDP data tables. Let me also check if the bulletins might be on different pages.\n\nActually, looking at the question more carefully - it asks about \"unannualized values\" that are \"reported as annual rate values rounded to the nearest tenths place\". This could mean:\n1. The unannualized quarterly growth rates (quarter-over-quarter), which when annualized become the reported values\n2. Or it could be referring to a specific presentation of the data\n\nLet me try a different approach and search online for this data. Actually wait - I can't do that. Let me think about this more carefully.\n\nThe key information in the documents is:\n- 2015 Q4: 0.7% (annual rate)\n- 2015 Q3: 2.0% (annual rate)\n- 2019 Q4: 2.1% (annual rate)\n- 2019 Q3: 2.1% (annual rate)\n\nThe treasury bulletins don't seem to have complete quarterly GDP data for all years from 2013-2019. Let me search more in the files or try to extract data from the text.\n \nI'm focusing on the Treasury Bulletin's \"Profile of the Economy\" section, which contains economic analysis but lacks detailed quarterly GDP tables. The data appears fragmented, with only partial information available for certain quarters. I'll need to dig deeper to find comprehensive GDP growth rates across the specified years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_56494a49714f425781ad3957","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let's search for GDP table data in the 2016 bulletin more systematically\nimport json\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2016_03.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nelements = data.get('document', {}).get('elements', [])\n\n# Look for table elements\nfor i, elem in enumerate(elements):\n    if isinstance(elem, dict) and elem.get('type') == 'table':\n        content = str(elem.get('content', ''))\n        # Check for numeric data\n        if any(x in content for x in ['2013', '2014', '2015', '2016']) and any(x in content.lower() for x in ['gdp', 'percent', 'quarter']):\n            print(f\"\\n=== Element {i} ===\")\n            print(content[:1500])\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
