{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346337-zKU8dTdkamnIAnd6C0u5","role":"assistant","created":1775346358,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Based on my analysis, the treasury bulletins don't contain the complete quarterly GDP data I need in a tabular format. They only contain commentary with limited quarterly GDP figures (e.g., Q4 2019: 2.1%). \n\nHowever, I can find the data I need from publicly available sources. The question asks about \"U.S. quarterly growth rates of the real GDP at 'unannualized' values that are actually reported as annual rate values rounded to the nearest tenths place from CY 2013-2019 inclusive.\"\n\nThis is BEA (Bureau of Economic Analysis) data. The GDP growth rates reported as \"annual rates\" in the treasury bulletins are what I need to analyze. The \"unannualized\" values reported as \"annual rate\" values typically refer to the quarter-over-quarter annualized growth rates.\n\nSince I can't find all the quarterly data in the treasury bulletins, let me try to find it from an online source, or I can use what I know about the historical GDP data.\n\nActually, let me re-read the question more carefully:\n- \"U.S. quarterly growth rates of the real GDP at 'unannualized' values that are actually reported as annual rate values\"\n- This refers to the \"percent change at annual rate\" which is how BEA reports quarterly GDP\n- These are seasonally-adjusted annualized rates (SAAR)\n- The values are \"rounded to the nearest tenths place\"\n\nI need to find quarterly growth rates for 2013-2019 and calculate the geometric mean for each year. Since I can't find all this data in the treasury bulletins, I'll need to look elsewhere.\n\nLet me check if there are any additional files or if I can access this data from the FRED API or other source.\n\nActually, wait - let me re-examine the problem. I should look for quarterly GDP data more carefully. The bulletins may contain this in a different location. Let me search for specific years and quarters.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_18fbd1ef05fa45249073e3f5","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me try to find all quarterly GDP data systematically\n# by looking for numbers next to quarters in the bulletin text\n\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2020_03.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Find patterns like \"Q1 2015\", \"Q2 2015\" etc with percentages\n# These should be near GDP data\n\n# Let me search for the complete set of quarterly GDP mentions\npatterns = [\n    # Q1 with percent\n    r'(Q1\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    r'(first quarter\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    # Q2 with percent  \n    r'(Q2\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    r'(second quarter\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    # Q3 with percent\n    r'(Q3\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    r'(third quarter\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    # Q4 with percent\n    r'(Q4\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n    r'(fourth quarter\\s*20[1-9][0-9])[^\\d]*(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*percent',\n]\n\nfor pattern in patterns:\n    matches = re.findall(pattern, content, re.IGNORECASE)\n    if matches:\n        print(f\"\\nPattern: {pattern[:50]}...\")\n        for m in matches[:10]:\n            print(f\"  {m}\")\n\n# Also search in 2016 bulletin\nprint(\"\\n\\n=== 2016 BULLETIN ===\")\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2016_03.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n    \nfor pattern in patterns:\n    matches = re.findall(pattern, content, re.IGNORECASE)\n    if matches:\n        print(f\"\\nPattern: {pattern[:50]}...\")\n        for m in matches[:10]:\n            print(f\"  {m}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
