{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775346380-es26kBIkAeRXNADjfPgh","role":"assistant","created":1775346392,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The BEA API requires an API key. Let me try another approach - let me look at historical data from FRED or try to find the data from a web search or calculate it from known data.\n\nActually, let me step back and think about this problem. The Treasury Bulletins do contain the GDP data but maybe in a different format. Let me check if there's more data by looking at different years and pages in the bulletins.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_40a6119e5b9e432daa92bd58","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me try a different approach - use known historical data for US GDP quarterly growth\n# These are \"unannualized\" values reported as \"annual rates\" - this is the standard\n# quarterly GDP growth rate that BEA publishes\n\n# According to Bureau of Economic Analysis data, here are the quarterly real GDP \n# growth rates (annualized/annual rate) for 2013-2019:\n\n# The data I found from the bulletins and known sources:\n# The values are percentages at annual rates\n\n# Let me compile the quarterly data from multiple sources and verify\n\n# First, let me extract more data from the bulletins by looking at specific pages\nimport re\n\n# The bulletins provide some data - let me look at more content\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2020_03.txt', 'r') as f:\n    c2020 = f.read()\n    \nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2016_03.txt', 'r') as f:\n    c2016 = f.read()\n\n# Look for ALL quarter-year-percent combinations in the text\n# For each year, find the quarters\n\nyears = ['2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019']\nquarters = ['Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4', 'first quarter', 'second quarter', 'third quarter', 'fourth quarter']\n\nfor year in years:\n    print(f\"\\n=== {year} ===\")\n    # Find text around this year with percent values\n    pattern = rf'{year}[^.]*?(\\d+\\.\\d+)\\s*(?:percent|%)'\n    matches = re.findall(pattern, c2020 + c2016, re.IGNORECASE)\n    print(f\"All percent values near {year}: {matches[:10]}\")\n    \n    # Also search for the quarter patterns\n    for q in quarters[:4]:  # Just Q1-Q4\n        q_pattern = rf'{q}[^{year}]{{0,50}}{year}[^0-9]{{0,10}}(\\d+\\.\\d+)'\n        q_matches = re.findall(q_pattern, c2020 + c2016, re.IGNORECASE)\n        if q_matches:\n            print(f\"  {q} {year}: {q_matches}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
